{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-65399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify ${sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify our expression by factoring it as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x & =({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x) & =(1)({sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "070a2bf9c6c8fb455c445c4397759daac4f1b028570d67a1cb1d55de54b4b9a8"} {"question" "q-65399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )+2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1)+2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression using $(2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta +2{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "070a2bf9c6c8fb455c445c4397759daac4f1b028570d67a1cb1d55de54b4b9a8"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha ={sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha -1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it out, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha (\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha \\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\alpha +\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\alpha +1}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "070a2bf9c6c8fb455c445c4397759daac4f1b028570d67a1cb1d55de54b4b9a8"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha "] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha "] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha +1"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡\\alpha "] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡\\alpha +1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-65410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x-1) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x & =(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x=(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "070a2bf9c6c8fb455c445c4397759daac4f1b028570d67a1cb1d55de54b4b9a8"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{4}"] ["math" "(1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x){tan}^{3}⁡x"] ["math" "(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{4}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){tan}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "070a2bf9c6c8fb455c445c4397759daac4f1b028570d67a1cb1d55de54b4b9a8"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c24597406f50b331ca83f63bb423711811556a10c3ae32948f0dc86"} {"question" "q-74162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053858/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2a9ad861c2459740